Root cause:
The bug occurs when the `PTE_MARKER_UFFD_WP` feature is not configured, yet the code paths that handle userfaultfd write protection (uffd_wp) are still reachable. This leads to warnings being triggered due to the presence of code that expects the feature to be available, resulting in potential inconsistencies and undefined behavior.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
#ifdef CONFIG_PTE_MARKER_UFFD_WP
if (pte_swp_uffd_wp_any(pte) && !(zap_flags & ZAP_FLAG_DROP_MARKER))
    set_huge_pte_at(mm, address, ptep, make_pte_marker(PTE_MARKER_UFFD_WP));
#endif
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the code that handles userfaultfd write protection (uffd_wp) is executed even when the `PTE_MARKER_UFFD_WP` feature is not configured. This leads to warnings being triggered since the code expects the feature to be available, resulting in potential inconsistencies and undefined behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
#ifdef CONFIG_PTE_MARKER_UFFD_WP
// Code related to handling uffd_wp markers
#endif
```
Reason:
The patch adds conditional compilation directives (`#ifdef CONFIG_PTE_MARKER_UFFD_WP`) around the code that handles the uffd_wp markers. This ensures that the code will not be compiled or executed if the `PTE_MARKER_UFFD_WP` feature is not configured, thus preventing the warnings and ensuring the code behaves correctly without the feature.


